            {
                "entry_id": "cf792429-9fc4-3d81-886d-b2fb79792da0",
                "word": "châtelaine",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4470006b-1f39-48d6-a989-363c5cdd7a23",
                        "entry_id": "cf792429-9fc4-3d81-886d-b2fb79792da0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "châtelaines"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "165dd957-49ae-3ed2-b52c-ba3d4e2731f1",
                        "entry_id": "cf792429-9fc4-3d81-886d-b2fb79792da0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chaîne attachée par un crochet à la ceinture d’une femme et à laquelle on suspend des bijoux, des clefs ou des ciseaux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cdb7d5aa-41dc-4384-9e35-cc1e6ff5f40f",
                                "sense_id": "165dd957-49ae-3ed2-b52c-ba3d4e2731f1",
                                "text": "Sur le cadre blanc de la glace assombrie et tachée, deux crochets de cuivre, où s’étaient suspendues les châtelaines des dames d’autrefois, s’offraient à l’envi pour recevoir ma montre, que j’eus soin de remonter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd423551-9c0b-4f7a-9f58-860fa7574b3c",
                                "sense_id": "165dd957-49ae-3ed2-b52c-ba3d4e2731f1",
                                "text": "Une femme mince, bien coiffée, les cheveux en casque à la mode d’autrefois, des ciseaux de couturière pendus à une « châtelaine » d’acier, sur son tablier noir."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5d042dab-5501-3a0a-9590-903c349d5377",
                        "entry_id": "cf792429-9fc4-3d81-886d-b2fb79792da0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans le costume masculin, chaîne ordinairement terminée par une médaille, qui est fixée à la montre et qu’on laisse pendre en dehors du gousset du gilet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a1dcf83e-92f2-43d9-9dfb-f2bfa2ba36c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "cf792429-9fc4-3d81-886d-b2fb79792da0",
                        "source_sense_id": "165dd957-49ae-3ed2-b52c-ba3d4e2731f1",
                        "source_sense_description": "Chaîne dans le costume féminin",
                        "target_lang_word": "chatelaine",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chatelaine",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af07bbf9-8339-38bd-88ca-e6a299d3ecd0",
                                        "entry_id": "664664a6-ca4c-33d3-98ba-f676ea54c3f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The mistress of a castle or large household."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd75161b-7be5-40b9-8fc6-5e33e66fe962",
                                                "sense_id": "af07bbf9-8339-38bd-88ca-e6a299d3ecd0",
                                                "text": "Gerard returned safely to his native land, and in the fantastic spirit of the times, he approached his own castle disguised as a pilgrim, intending to himself and his Chatelaine, the delight of a romantic surprise. […] He accordingly repaired, in the silent hour of midnight, when the castle was wrapped in sleep, to the well-remembered chamber of the Chatelaine. She was not alone. A handsome young page supplied the place of her long-absent lord. In the excess of his rage, Gerard killed his wife on the spot, but reserved the page for a more lingering revenge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5e80a57-3d6f-4afc-ad46-af7e28bde829",
                                                "sense_id": "af07bbf9-8339-38bd-88ca-e6a299d3ecd0",
                                                "text": "[A] detachment of the Imperial army, under Francis Wesselény, was ordered to attack the castle. Having made the most elaborate preparations, he summoned the garrison to surrender; the refusal was haughty and uncompromising, and, to the surprise of Wesselény, dictated by the Chatelaine herself, who personally conducted its defence. To be foiled by a woman, little suited his proud nature; but all efforts to effect a breach in the massive walls of the stronghold were ineffectual, and every attack gallantly repulsed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d89fe34a-a504-46aa-a199-6bdf8adf5bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "af07bbf9-8339-38bd-88ca-e6a299d3ecd0",
                                                "text": "Cars passed her on the road; the people of the quarry town knew her and bowed to her; she was considered the chatelaine of the countryside, as her mother had been long ago."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                        "entry_id": "664664a6-ca4c-33d3-98ba-f676ea54c3f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A chain or clasp worn at the waist by women with handkerchief, keys, etc., attached, supposed to resemble the chain of keys once worn by medieval chatelaines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ecfc5a8-4517-46cd-91d0-4bac33b8c9b1",
                                                "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                                "text": "This elegant little appendage to the dress, large enough to contain a handkerchief and purse, is deserving of being as generally adopted in the United States as it has recently been in Paris. […] Both sides of the Chatelaine are embroidered alike. […] The hook attaches this Chatelaine to the wristband."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec0115d8-d713-44d1-9a5c-b68db0a3177d",
                                                "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                                "text": "The latest fashion is to wear watches suspended from the chatelaine. The chatelaine is short, and ornamented with charms."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4abd3edd-d4a2-4949-b481-c783ed653caf",
                                                "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                                "text": "If we examine the relics of antique chatelaines in the Hotel Cluny and other museums, we observe serviceable articles, as scissors, étui, pomander-box (for sudden illness), and keys that would break the delicate fingers of a modern belle to handle. For the chatelaine was then responsible for the health and welfare of her people in times of war and of peace; her duties were as varied as they were unceasing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4cfcd83-4444-44e4-8ee2-dac35d64497a",
                                                "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                                "text": "Châtelaines are generally lovely things, but for our part we can never look upon them without feeling them to be more or less of a reproach to our modern want of thrift."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45a0e754-bb7b-4629-ad4e-1afeecb32a7a",
                                                "sense_id": "61acee2e-b2af-336f-a9df-b2030c9de67b",
                                                "text": "The famous novelist was dressed in a badly fitting sleazy purple dress and a shapeless Napoleonic hat, with gloves and a long chatelaine; but the costume only heightened her air of distinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "179890da-fa79-35bd-9258-c772bf7cf6fa",
                                        "entry_id": "664664a6-ca4c-33d3-98ba-f676ea54c3f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A similar thing in miniature attached to a watchchain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bb39dd5-ae38-48fa-a668-eb290e40a28d",
                                                "sense_id": "179890da-fa79-35bd-9258-c772bf7cf6fa",
                                                "text": "A French fashion is now busy investing the large body of French gentlemen with Chatelaines. These do not hang, as with English ladies, from the waist, but from the waistcoat pocket. They are generally attached to the watch—or, supposing the gentleman has no such useful appendage for killing time, then they are fastened to the waistcoat-button, and allowed to dangle gracefully therefrom."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a9ca0ba-7dde-45db-ab21-679d2ed2be94",
                                                "sense_id": "179890da-fa79-35bd-9258-c772bf7cf6fa",
                                                "text": "The Swiss jewellery chiefly consisted of châtelaines or watch pendants, having no very distinct style or character, but embracing examples of all styles, both ancient and modern; […] One of the chief attractions in the collection were the examples of châtelaines attached to watch cases, ornamented in a similar style."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
